IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpa-dates`

-- Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) -- the rules: Chapter 1 (application, definitions), Chapter 2 (overarching purpose and
-- overarching obligations, their reach and sanctions), Chapter 4 Parts 4.1 to 4.4 and 4.6 (certification, case
-- management, discovery, summary judgment, expert evidence) and Chapter 5 (appropriate dispute resolution), so far as
-- they give a party a fact test.
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in cpa-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("does not apply", "means",
-- "must not", "may not", "except by leave", "unless", "if" conditions that fail, a period the text fixes); or NOTHING
-- where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The court's judgments ("satisfied",
-- "considers appropriate", "reasonable", "interests of justice", leave, orders) are inputs: the answer is conditional on
-- them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Civil Procedure
-- Act 2010, Version No. 022 (30 September 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the
-- authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the
-- Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Procedure Act 2010`

§§ `Chapter 1 -- which proceedings the Act applies to (ss 3, 4)`

-- s 3: "court means the following courts -- (a) the Supreme Court; (b) the County Court; (c) the Magistrates' Court".
-- s 4(3): "This Act does not apply to any proceeding in VCAT."
DECLARE `Court` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court`
    `the County Court`
    `the Magistrates' Court`
    `VCAT`
    `another court or tribunal`

-- s 4(2): "This Act does not apply to proceedings under the following Acts -- ..." (paragraphs (a) to (l)).
DECLARE `Act the proceeding is under` IS ONE OF
    `none of the Acts section 4(2) lists`
    `the Family Violence Protection Act 2008`
    `the Personal Safety Intervention Orders Act 2010`
    `the Confiscation Act 1997`
    `the Proceeds of Crime Act 1987 or 2002 of the Commonwealth`
    `the Crimes (Mental Impairment and Unfitness to be Tried) Act 1997`
    `the Criminal Organisations Control Act 2012`
    `the Children, Youth and Families Act 2005`
    `the Coroners Act 2008`
    `the Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1996`
    `the Sentencing Act 1991`
    `the Serious Offenders Act 2018`
    `Part 3A of the Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 1998`
    `the National Domestic Violence Order Scheme Act 2016`
    `the Youth Justice Act 2024`

-- s 3: "civil proceeding means any proceeding in a court other than a criminal proceeding or quasi-criminal proceeding".
-- s 4(1): "Subject to this section, this Act applies to all civil proceedings." (4): "This Act does not apply to any
-- proceeding under a prescribed Act." (No regulations prescribing an Act are deposited: asked as a fact.)
GIVEN `the court`                   IS A `Court`
      `criminal or quasi-criminal`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act it is under`         IS AN `Act the proceeding is under`
      `under a prescribed Act`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 3, 4 -- the Act applies to the proceeding` `the court` `criminal or quasi-criminal` `the Act it is under` `under a prescribed Act` MEANS
    IF `criminal or quasi-criminal`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the court`
         WHEN `VCAT` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `another court or tribunal` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the Act it is under`
            WHEN `none of the Acts section 4(2) lists` THEN
                IF `under a prescribed Act`
                THEN JUST FALSE
                ELSE JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Chapter 2 -- to whom the overarching obligations apply (s 10)`

DECLARE `Role in the proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `a party`
    `a witness, not as an expert`
    `an expert witness`
    `a person who gives a party financial or other assistance`

-- s 3: "overarching obligations means the obligations set out in sections 16 to 26".
DECLARE `Overarching obligation` IS ONE OF
    `s 16 the paramount duty to further the administration of justice`
    `s 17 to act honestly`
    `s 18 to make no claim or response without a proper basis`
    `s 19 to take only steps necessary to resolve or determine the dispute`
    `s 20 to cooperate with the parties and the court`
    `s 21 not to mislead or deceive`
    `s 22 to use reasonable endeavours to resolve the dispute by agreement`
    `s 23 to use reasonable endeavours to narrow the issues in dispute`
    `s 24 to use reasonable endeavours to keep costs reasonable and proportionate`
    `s 25 to use reasonable endeavours to act promptly and minimise delay`
    `s 26 to disclose the existence of critical documents`

-- s 10(3): "The overarching obligations (other than the overarching obligations specified in sections 18, 19, 22 and 26)
-- apply to any expert witness in a civil proceeding."
GIVEN `the obligation` IS AN `Overarching obligation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(3) -- the obligation is one an expert witness is spared` `the obligation` IF
    CONSIDER `the obligation`
    WHEN `s 18 to make no claim or response without a proper basis` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 19 to take only steps necessary to resolve or determine the dispute` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 22 to use reasonable endeavours to resolve the dispute by agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 26 to disclose the existence of critical documents` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 10(1): "The overarching obligations apply to -- (a) any person who is a party; ... (d) any person who provides
-- financial assistance or other assistance to any party in so far as that person exercises any direct control, indirect
-- control or any influence over the conduct of the civil proceeding or of a party in respect of that civil proceeding,
-- including ... an insurer; ... any litigation funder." (2): "Subject to subsection (3), the overarching obligations do
-- not apply to any witness in a civil proceeding." (3): above.
-- A helper with no control or influence: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording* ("in so far as"; fork F1).
-- An expert witness and one of ss 18, 19, 22, 26: JUST FALSE ("other than"; fork F2).
GIVEN `my role`                                  IS A `Role in the proceeding`
      `the obligation`                           IS AN `Overarching obligation`
      `I exercise control or influence`          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10 -- the overarching obligation applies to me` `my role` `the obligation` `I exercise control or influence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `a party` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a witness, not as an expert` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an expert witness` THEN
        IF `s 10(3) -- the obligation is one an expert witness is spared` `the obligation`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person who gives a party financial or other assistance` THEN
        IF `I exercise control or influence`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Chapter 2 -- the overarching obligations of a party (ss 18, 19, 22, 23, 26, 27)`

-- s 18: "A person to whom the overarching obligations apply must not make any claim or make a response to any claim in a
-- civil proceeding that -- (a) is frivolous; or (b) is vexatious; or (c) is an abuse of process; or (d) does not, on the
-- factual and legal material available to the person at the time of making the claim or responding to the claim, as the
-- case requires, have a proper basis."
-- A claim or response outside (a) to (d): NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording* (s 18 neither forbids nor permits it).
GIVEN `frivolous`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `vexatious`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `an abuse of process`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has a proper basis`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18 -- I must not make the claim or response` `frivolous` `vexatious` `an abuse of process` `it has a proper basis` MEANS
    IF `frivolous` OR `vexatious` OR `an abuse of process` OR (NOT `it has a proper basis`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 19: "For the purpose of avoiding undue delay and expense, a person to whom the overarching obligations apply must not
-- take any step in connection with any claim or response to any claim in a civil proceeding unless the person reasonably
-- believes that the step is necessary to facilitate the resolution or determination of the proceeding."
-- The "unless" met: JUST FALSE (fork F3).
GIVEN `I reasonably believe the step is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 -- I must not take the step` `I reasonably believe the step is necessary` MEANS
    IF `I reasonably believe the step is necessary`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 22: "... must use reasonable endeavours to resolve a dispute by agreement between the persons in dispute, including, if
-- appropriate, by appropriate dispute resolution, unless -- (a) it is not in the interests of justice to do so; or (b) the
-- dispute is of such a nature that only judicial determination is appropriate."
GIVEN `not in the interests of justice`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `only judicial determination is appropriate`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22 -- I must try to resolve the dispute by agreement` `not in the interests of justice` `only judicial determination is appropriate` MEANS
    IF `not in the interests of justice` OR `only judicial determination is appropriate`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 23: "If a person to whom the overarching obligations apply cannot resolve a dispute wholly by agreement, the person must
-- use reasonable endeavours to -- (a) resolve by agreement any issues in dispute which can be resolved in that way; and
-- (b) narrow the scope of the remaining issues in dispute -- unless -- (c) it is not in the interests of justice to do so;
-- or (d) the dispute is of such a nature that only judicial determination is appropriate."
-- The "if" unmet (the dispute resolved wholly by agreement): JUST FALSE (fork F4).
GIVEN `the dispute is resolved wholly by agreement`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `not in the interests of justice`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `only judicial determination is appropriate`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23 -- I must try to narrow the issues` `the dispute is resolved wholly by agreement` `not in the interests of justice` `only judicial determination is appropriate` MEANS
    IF `the dispute is resolved wholly by agreement`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `not in the interests of justice` OR `only judicial determination is appropriate`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 26(1): "Subject to subsection (3), a person to whom the overarching obligations apply must disclose to each party the
-- existence of all documents that are, or have been, in that person's possession, custody or control -- (a) of which the
-- person is aware; and (b) which the person considers, or ought reasonably consider, are critical to the resolution of
-- the dispute." (3): "Subsection (1) does not apply to any document which is protected from disclosure -- (a) on the
-- grounds of privilege which has not been expressly or impliedly waived; or (b) under any Act (including any Commonwealth
-- Act) or other law."
-- A document outside (1): NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording* (s 26 does not require it; discovery may, s 26(4)(b)).
GIVEN `in my possession, custody or control, now or before`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am aware of it`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is critical to the resolution of the dispute`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `privileged, privilege not waived`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `protected from disclosure by another law`              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26 -- I must disclose the existence of the document` `in my possession, custody or control, now or before` `I am aware of it` `it is critical to the resolution of the dispute` `privileged, privilege not waived` `protected from disclosure by another law` MEANS
    IF `privileged, privilege not waived` OR `protected from disclosure by another law`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `in my possession, custody or control, now or before` AND `I am aware of it` AND `it is critical to the resolution of the dispute`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- s 26(2): "Disclosure under subsection (1) must occur at -- (a) the earliest reasonable time after the person becomes aware
-- of the existence of the document; or (b) such other time as a court may direct." The earliest reasonable time is a
-- judgment, so the day it falls on is an input. The rule runs on plain days from the day the person became aware.
DECLARE `Discloser` IS ONE OF
    `the person who must disclose`

DECLARE `Disclosure act` IS ONE OF
    `disclose the existence of the document to each party`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Discloser` `Disclosure act`
`s 26(2) -- the document must be disclosed by the time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the person who must disclose`
    MUST `disclose the existence of the document to each party`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person who must disclose` BECAUSE "the existence of the document was not disclosed at the earliest reasonable time or the time the court directed (s 26(2)); the court may take the contravention into account (s 28) and make orders against the person (s 29)"

-- The helper that runs the duty over what happened (in the shape of the Supreme Court Act 1986 encoding's helper). On the
-- stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED means in time
-- and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it now would still be in time. It takes a
-- DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `What became of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open`

GIVEN `the rule`                    IS A DEONTIC `Discloser` `Disclosure act`
      `the act has been done`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done`   IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`                IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of the disclosure duty` `the rule` `the act has been done` `the time the act was done` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the person who must disclose` `disclose the existence of the document to each party` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the person who must disclose` `disclose the existence of the document to each party` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

GIVEN `the day I became aware`                IS A DATE
      `the court directed a time`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the court directed`            IS A DATE
      `the earliest reasonable day`           IS A DATE
      `I have disclosed it`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I disclosed it`                IS A DATE
      `today`                                 IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`s 26(2) -- what became of my disclosure` `the day I became aware` `the court directed a time` `the day the court directed` `the earliest reasonable day` `I have disclosed it` `the day I disclosed it` `today` MEANS
    `what became of the disclosure duty` (`s 26(2) -- the document must be disclosed by the time` (`the days from` `the day I became aware` `to` `the last day`)) `I have disclosed it` (`the days from` `the day I became aware` `to` `the day I disclosed it`) (`the days from` `the day I became aware` `to` `today`)
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS
            IF `the court directed a time`
            THEN `the day the court directed`
            ELSE `the earliest reasonable day`

-- s 27(1): a person who receives documents or information disclosed under s 26 "is subject to an obligation not to use the
-- information or documents, or permit [them] to be used, for a purpose other than in connection with the civil
-- proceeding." (2): contravention "constitutes contempt of court". (3): "A person -- (a) may agree in writing to the use
-- ...; or (b) may be released from the obligation ... by leave of the court."
GIVEN `the discloser agreed in writing`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court released me`             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27 -- I may use the disclosed documents for another purpose` `the discloser agreed in writing` `the court released me` MEANS
    IF `the discloser agreed in writing` OR `the court released me`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 27(4): "... any information or documents exchanged in compliance with the overarching obligation in section 26 is
-- required to be discovered in the civil proceeding to be admissible in that proceeding."
-- Discovered: NOTHING-kind *points outside the text* (the rules of evidence decide admissibility).
GIVEN `it has been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(4) -- the exchanged document can be admitted` `it has been discovered` MEANS
    IF `it has been discovered`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Chapter 2 -- sanctions (ss 29, 30, 31)`

-- s 29(1): "If a court is satisfied that, on the balance of probabilities, a person has contravened any overarching
-- obligation, the court may make any order it considers appropriate in the interests of justice including ..." costs,
-- immediate payment, compensation (with penalty interest, or no or reduced interest), remedial steps, a bar on steps.
GIVEN `the court is satisfied I contravened an overarching obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29 -- the court may make an order against me` `the court is satisfied I contravened an overarching obligation` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied I contravened an overarching obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 29(2)(a): an order may be made on the application of "(i) any party to the civil proceeding; or (ii) any other person
-- who, in the opinion of the court, has a sufficient interest in the proceeding". s 30(2): "must be made prior to the
-- finalisation of the civil proceeding ... (excluding any period for appeals)". (3): "if an order, including an order in
-- respect of costs, is made after the date of finalisation ..., the date of making of the last of the orders is taken to
-- be the date of finalisation". s 31(1): "Despite section 30(2), a person may apply to the court for an extension of
-- time"; (2): "The court may grant an extension ... if satisfied that the person making the application was not aware of
-- the contravention ... until after the end of the period specified in section 30(2)." (3): by a party or a person with a
-- sufficient interest.
DECLARE `Where I stand on a section 29 application` IS ONE OF
    `I may apply now, before the proceeding is finalised`
    `out of time, but I may apply for an extension, which the court may grant because I did not know in time`
    `out of time, and the court has extended the time: I may apply`
    `out of time, and no extension can be granted because I knew of the contravention in time`

-- Not a party and no sufficient interest: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording* (s 29(2) lists who may apply without
-- "only"; the court may still act on its own motion).
GIVEN `I am a party or have a sufficient interest`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding has been finalised`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was unaware of the contravention until after`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has extended the time`                     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Where I stand on a section 29 application`
`ss 30, 31 -- where I stand on applying under section 29` `I am a party or have a sufficient interest` `the proceeding has been finalised` `I was unaware of the contravention until after` `the court has extended the time` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am a party or have a sufficient interest`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `the proceeding has been finalised`)
         THEN JUST `I may apply now, before the proceeding is finalised`
         ELSE IF (NOT `I was unaware of the contravention until after`)
              THEN JUST `out of time, and no extension can be granted because I knew of the contravention in time`
              ELSE IF `the court has extended the time`
                   THEN JUST `out of time, and the court has extended the time: I may apply`
                   ELSE JUST `out of time, but I may apply for an extension, which the court may grant because I did not know in time`

§§ `Chapter 4 Part 4.1 -- certification on commencement (ss 3, 41, 42, 44, 45)`

-- s 3: "substantive document means -- (a) ... (q) ... but does not include -- (r) ... (z) ...".
DECLARE `Kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `an originating motion`
    `a writ with a statement of claim, or with a statement of the nature of the claim, its cause and the relief sought`
    `a writ with neither`
    `a complaint`
    `a defence or a notice of defence`
    `a reply`
    `a counterclaim`
    `an answer to a counterclaim, or a response to such an answer`
    `a claim by third party notice, or a response to one`
    `a claim by fourth or subsequent party notice, or a response to one`
    `an application under section 93(4)(d) of the Transport Accident Act 1986, or a response to one`
    `an affidavit, summons or application that commences the proceeding or is my first response in it`
    `an affidavit, summons or application that does neither`
    `a notice of referral under section 80 of the Land Acquisition and Compensation Act 1986, or a response to one`
    `a claim for contribution under Part IV of the Wrongs Act 1958, or a response to one`
    `an application for leave to appear and defend under the Instruments Act 1958`
    `a claim for preliminary discovery`
    `a summons for taxation of costs`
    `an application for punishment for contempt of court`
    `an application for a rehearing under section 110 of the Magistrates' Court Act 1989`
    `an application under section 299 of the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013`
    `an application under section 24 of the Second-Hand Dealers and Pawnbrokers Act 1989`
    `an application under section 83 of the Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004`
    `a process that commences an appeal, or the first response to an appeal`
    `a process that commences proceedings under the Corporations Act or the ASIC Act, or the first response to one`
    `an originating motion filed under Chapter III of the Rules of the Supreme Court`
    `any other document`

-- A "means" definition with its own exclusions: JUST TRUE for (a) to (q), JUST FALSE otherwise. The exclusions (u) and
-- (z) are taken over (m) and (a) where they meet (finding 3).
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Kind of document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- the document is a substantive document` `the document` IF
    CONSIDER `the document`
    WHEN `an originating motion` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a writ with a statement of claim, or with a statement of the nature of the claim, its cause and the relief sought` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a complaint` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a defence or a notice of defence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a reply` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a counterclaim` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an answer to a counterclaim, or a response to such an answer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a claim by third party notice, or a response to one` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a claim by fourth or subsequent party notice, or a response to one` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an application under section 93(4)(d) of the Transport Accident Act 1986, or a response to one` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an affidavit, summons or application that commences the proceeding or is my first response in it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notice of referral under section 80 of the Land Acquisition and Compensation Act 1986, or a response to one` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a claim for contribution under Part IV of the Wrongs Act 1958, or a response to one` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an application for leave to appear and defend under the Instruments Act 1958` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a claim for preliminary discovery` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 41(1): "Each party must personally certify that the party has read and understood the overarching obligations and the
-- paramount duty." (3): a litigation guardian or similar representative "may make" it. (4): "if a party has no meaningful
-- control over the conduct of a civil proceeding by virtue of a statute or a contract of insurance, the person in
-- control ... may make" it (example: an insurer). (5): "a party who is represented by a legal practitioner is not
-- required to make the overarching obligations certification if -- (a) the party is currently involved, or has been
-- involved, in more than one civil proceeding and has personally made the overarching obligations certification in other
-- civil proceedings in the same jurisdiction within -- (i) a period specified by rules of court; or (ii) if no period is
-- specified by rules of court, 2 years prior to the current proceeding; and (b) the legal practitioner of that party
-- certifies, in accordance with the rules of court, as to the matters specified in paragraph (a)."
DECLARE `Who makes the overarching obligations certification` IS ONE OF
    `I must certify personally`
    `my litigation guardian or similar representative may certify for me`
    `the person in control under the statute or insurance contract, for example my insurer, may certify for me`
    `I need not certify, because my lawyer certifies that I certified in another proceeding within the period`

-- The s 41(5) window: on or after the day the period (rules-of-court months, or 24 months) before the current proceeding
-- began, and not after that day (forks F5, F6).
GIVEN `the day I last certified personally elsewhere`      IS A DATE
      `the day the current proceeding was commenced`       IS A DATE
      `the months the rules of court specify`              IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41(5)(a) -- my earlier certification is within the period` `the day I last certified personally elsewhere` `the day the current proceeding was commenced` `the months the rules of court specify` IF
        (NOT (`the day I last certified personally elsewhere` `is before` (`the date` `the months counted back` `months before` `the day the current proceeding was commenced`)))
    AND (NOT (`the day I last certified personally elsewhere` `is after` `the day the current proceeding was commenced`))
    WHERE
        `the months counted back` MEANS
            IF `the months the rules of court specify` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN `the months the rules of court specify`
            ELSE 24

GIVEN `I have a litigation guardian or similar representative`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have no meaningful control because of a statute or insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am represented by a legal practitioner`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have certified personally in another proceeding in the same jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I last certified personally elsewhere`                 IS A DATE
      `the day the current proceeding was commenced`                  IS A DATE
      `the months the rules of court specify`                         IS A NUMBER
      `my lawyer certifies those matters`                             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who makes the overarching obligations certification`
`s 41 -- who makes my overarching obligations certification` `I have a litigation guardian or similar representative` `I have no meaningful control because of a statute or insurance` `I am represented by a legal practitioner` `I have certified personally in another proceeding in the same jurisdiction` `the day I last certified personally elsewhere` `the day the current proceeding was commenced` `the months the rules of court specify` `my lawyer certifies those matters` MEANS
    IF     `I am represented by a legal practitioner`
       AND `I have certified personally in another proceeding in the same jurisdiction`
       AND `s 41(5)(a) -- my earlier certification is within the period` `the day I last certified personally elsewhere` `the day the current proceeding was commenced` `the months the rules of court specify`
       AND `my lawyer certifies those matters`
    THEN `I need not certify, because my lawyer certifies that I certified in another proceeding within the period`
    ELSE IF `I have no meaningful control because of a statute or insurance`
         THEN `the person in control under the statute or insurance contract, for example my insurer, may certify for me`
         ELSE IF `I have a litigation guardian or similar representative`
              THEN `my litigation guardian or similar representative may certify for me`
              ELSE `I must certify personally`

-- s 42(1): "A legal practitioner acting for or on behalf of a party to the proceeding must file a proper basis
-- certification ... (a) on the filing of a party's first substantive document ...; (b) on the filing of any subsequent
-- substantive document ... which -- (i) adds or substitutes a party; or (ii) makes, adds or substitutes a claim or cause
-- of action; or (iii) makes, adds or substitutes a substantive defence or substantive matter by way of response or reply;
-- or (iv) makes, adds or substitutes a material allegation denial or non-admission of fact or law; or (v) makes any
-- significant amendment ...; (c) as provided for by rules of court; (d) as directed by the court". (1C): not required
-- where the rules exempt the document as administrative in nature. (4): "If a party is not represented by a legal
-- practitioner -- (a) the proper basis certification must be completed personally by that party".
DECLARE `Document being filed` IS ONE OF
    `my first substantive document`
    `a later substantive document that adds or substitutes a party`
    `a later substantive document that makes, adds or substitutes a claim or cause of action`
    `a later substantive document that makes, adds or substitutes a substantive defence, response or reply`
    `a later substantive document that makes, adds or substitutes a material allegation, denial or non-admission`
    `a later substantive document that makes a significant amendment to an earlier one`
    `a later substantive document that does none of these`
    `a document that is not a substantive document`

DECLARE `Who files the proper basis certification` IS ONE OF
    `my legal practitioner must file it`
    `I must complete and file it personally`
    `no one: the rules exempt the document as administrative`

GIVEN `the document being filed` IS A `Document being filed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 42(1)(a), (b) -- the document calls for a proper basis certification` `the document being filed` IF
    CONSIDER `the document being filed`
    WHEN `a later substantive document that does none of these` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a document that is not a substantive document` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Outside (a) to (d): NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording* (s 42 requires none; the rules of court may, (c)).
GIVEN `the document being filed`                  IS A `Document being filed`
      `the rules or the court require one`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rules exempt it as administrative`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am represented by a legal practitioner`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who files the proper basis certification`
`s 42 -- who files the proper basis certification` `the document being filed` `the rules or the court require one` `the rules exempt it as administrative` `I am represented by a legal practitioner` MEANS
    IF `the rules exempt it as administrative`
    THEN JUST `no one: the rules exempt the document as administrative`
    ELSE IF `s 42(1)(a), (b) -- the document calls for a proper basis certification` `the document being filed` OR `the rules or the court require one`
         THEN IF `I am represented by a legal practitioner`
              THEN JUST `my legal practitioner must file it`
              ELSE JUST `I must complete and file it personally`
         ELSE NOTHING

-- s 44(1): "if as a matter of urgency a document is required to be filed ..., a party ... or a legal practitioner ...
-- may file the document without complying with the applicable certification provision of this Part." (2): the
-- certification must then be filed "as soon as practicable after filing the document".
GIVEN `the filing is urgent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 -- I may file now and certify later` `the filing is urgent` MEANS
    IF `the filing is urgent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 45: "Unless a court otherwise orders, a court may not prevent the commencement of civil proceedings in the court or the
-- filing of any substantive document by a party ... merely because of a failure to comply with any certification
-- requirement under this Part." The "unless" met (the court has so ordered): JUST TRUE (fork F7).
GIVEN `the court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45 -- the court may stop my filing for want of certification` `the court has ordered otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the court has ordered otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Chapter 4 Part 4.2 -- contravening a case management order (s 51)`

DECLARE `Side` IS ONE OF
    `a plaintiff`
    `a defendant`

-- s 51: "If a person to whom a direction has been given or to whom an order made under this Part applies contravenes the
-- direction or order, the court may do any one or more of the following -- (a) dismiss the civil proceeding ...; (b)
-- strike out or limit any claim made by a plaintiff; (c) strike out or limit any defence or part of a defence filed by a
-- defendant, and give judgment accordingly; (d) strike out or amend any document filed by the person ...; (e) disallow or
-- reject any evidence that the person has adduced or seeks to adduce; (f) direct the person to pay the whole or part of
-- the costs of another party or person; (g) make any other order or give any other direction".
DECLARE `Case management sanction` IS ONE OF
    `dismiss the proceeding, or a cause of action or claim in it`
    `strike out or limit my claim`
    `strike out or limit my defence and give judgment accordingly`
    `strike out or amend a document I filed`
    `disallow or reject evidence I adduced or seek to adduce`
    `direct me to pay costs of another party or person`
    `make any other order or direction it considers appropriate`

-- No contravention: JUST FALSE ("If ... contravenes"; this section gives no power on these facts, s 53 keeps others).
-- My claim when I am a defendant, my defence when I am a plaintiff: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*.
GIVEN `I contravened the direction or order`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `my side`                                IS A `Side`
      `the sanction`                           IS A `Case management sanction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51 -- the court may impose the sanction on me` `I contravened the direction or order` `my side` `the sanction` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I contravened the direction or order`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the sanction`
         WHEN `strike out or limit my claim` THEN
            CONSIDER `my side`
            WHEN `a plaintiff` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `a defendant` THEN NOTHING
         WHEN `strike out or limit my defence and give judgment accordingly` THEN
            CONSIDER `my side`
            WHEN `a defendant` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `a plaintiff` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Chapter 4 Part 4.3 -- discovery (ss 55A, 56, 57)`

-- s 55A(4): "if an order is made or a direction is given under subsection (1), the party providing documents ..., at that
-- party's own expense, may exclude any privileged documents prior to providing the documents". (5): "A party who excludes
-- any privileged documents ... must provide to the other party a list of the documents for which privilege is claimed which
-- specifies the grounds on which privilege is claimed."
-- No s 55A order: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*. Nothing excluded: JUST FALSE ("a party who excludes", read as
-- a "where" condition; fork F8).
GIVEN `the court ordered me to provide all my documents under section 55A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55A(4) -- I may hold back privileged documents` `the court ordered me to provide all my documents under section 55A` MEANS
    IF `the court ordered me to provide all my documents under section 55A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the court ordered me to provide all my documents under section 55A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I held back privileged documents`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55A(5) -- I must give a list of the privileged documents` `the court ordered me to provide all my documents under section 55A` `I held back privileged documents` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the court ordered me to provide all my documents under section 55A`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `I held back privileged documents`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 56(1): "A court may make any order or give any direction it considers appropriate if the court finds that there has
-- been -- (a) a failure to comply with discovery obligations; or (b) a failure to comply with any order or direction of
-- the court in relation to discovery; or (c) conduct intended to delay, frustrate or avoid discovery of discoverable
-- documents." (2) lists orders; (b), (c) and (j) are against the person or party "responsible".
DECLARE `Discovery finding` IS ONE OF
    `no such finding`
    `a failure to comply with discovery obligations`
    `a failure to comply with an order or direction about discovery`
    `conduct intended to delay, frustrate or avoid discovery`

DECLARE `Discovery sanction` IS ONE OF
    `that proceedings for contempt of court be initiated`
    `adjourn the proceeding, with the costs of the adjournment borne by me`
    `costs orders against me, including indemnity costs`
    `prevent me from taking a step in the proceeding`
    `prohibit or limit the use of documents in evidence`
    `take facts as established`
    `award compensation for loss arising out of the conduct`
    `draw an adverse inference from the conduct`
    `compel a person to give evidence about the conduct`
    `dismiss part of my claim or defence`
    `any other order or direction it considers appropriate`

GIVEN `the sanction` IS A `Discovery sanction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 56(2) -- the sanction is aimed at the person responsible` `the sanction` IF
    CONSIDER `the sanction`
    WHEN `adjourn the proceeding, with the costs of the adjournment borne by me` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `costs orders against me, including indemnity costs` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `dismiss part of my claim or defence` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- No finding: JUST FALSE ("if the court finds"). Not responsible and a sanction (2)(b), (c) or (j) aims at the person
-- responsible: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*.
GIVEN `the court's finding`        IS A `Discovery finding`
      `I am responsible for it`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sanction`               IS A `Discovery sanction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56 -- the court may impose the discovery sanction on me` `the court's finding` `I am responsible for it` `the sanction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the court's finding`
    WHEN `no such finding` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `s 56(2) -- the sanction is aimed at the person responsible` `the sanction` AND (NOT `I am responsible for it`)
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 57: "Unless a court orders otherwise, any party to a civil proceeding may cross-examine or seek leave to conduct an
-- oral examination of the deponent of an affidavit of documents prepared by or on behalf of any other party ... if there
-- is a reasonable basis for the belief that the other party may be -- (a) misinterpreting the party's discovery
-- obligations; or (b) failing to disclose discoverable documents."
GIVEN `there is a reasonable basis for the belief`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has ordered otherwise`             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57 -- I may cross-examine the deponent of the other side's affidavit of documents` `there is a reasonable basis for the belief` `the court has ordered otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the court has ordered otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `there is a reasonable basis for the belief`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Chapter 4 Part 4.4 -- summary judgment (ss 60 to 64)`

-- s 60: "a reference -- (a) to a plaintiff includes a reference to a plaintiff by counterclaim; and (b) to a defendant
-- includes a reference to a defendant by counterclaim."
DECLARE `Side for summary judgment` IS ONE OF
    `a plaintiff, or a plaintiff by counterclaim`
    `a defendant, or a defendant by counterclaim`
    `another party, for example a third party`

-- s 61: "A plaintiff ... may apply ... for summary judgment ... on the ground that a defendant's defence or part of that
-- defence has no real prospect of success." s 62: "A defendant ... may apply ... on the ground that a plaintiff's claim or
-- part of that claim has no real prospect of success." Another party: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording* (the
-- rules of court may give a power, s 65).
GIVEN `my side` IS A `Side for summary judgment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 61, 62 -- I may apply for summary judgment` `my side` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my side`
    WHEN `another party, for example a third party` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Who moves for summary judgment` IS ONE OF
    `the other side applied`
    `the court of its own motion`

-- s 63(1): "Subject to section 64, a court may give summary judgment in any civil proceeding if satisfied that a claim, a
-- defence or a counterclaim or part of [it] ... has no real prospect of success." (2): "(a) on the application of a
-- plaintiff ...; (b) on the application of a defendant ...; (c) on the court's own motion, if satisfied that it is
-- desirable to summarily dispose of the civil proceeding." s 64: "Despite anything to the contrary in this Part ..., a
-- court may order that a civil proceeding proceed to trial if the court is satisfied that, despite there being no real
-- prospect of success the civil proceeding should not be disposed of summarily because -- (a) it is not in the interests
-- of justice to do so; or (b) the dispute is of such a nature that only a full hearing on the merits is appropriate."
-- An order under s 64 made: JUST FALSE (fork F9).
GIVEN `the court is satisfied my case has no real prospect of success`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `who moves`                                                     IS A `Who moves for summary judgment`
      `the court is satisfied summary disposal is desirable`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has ordered the proceeding to trial under section 64` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 63, 64 -- the court may give summary judgment against me` `the court is satisfied my case has no real prospect of success` `who moves` `the court is satisfied summary disposal is desirable` `the court has ordered the proceeding to trial under section 64` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the court is satisfied my case has no real prospect of success`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the court has ordered the proceeding to trial under section 64`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `who moves`
              WHEN `the other side applied` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `the court of its own motion` THEN
                  IF `the court is satisfied summary disposal is desirable`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `not in the interests of justice to dispose summarily`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `only a full hearing on the merits is appropriate`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64 -- the court may send my proceeding to trial despite no real prospect` `not in the interests of justice to dispose summarily` `only a full hearing on the merits is appropriate` MEANS
    IF `not in the interests of justice to dispose summarily` OR `only a full hearing on the merits is appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Chapter 4 Part 4.6 -- expert evidence (ss 65G, 65J, 65L, 65N, 65O, 65P)`

-- s 65G(1): "Unless rules of court otherwise provide or the court otherwise orders, a party must seek direction from the
-- court as soon as practicable if the party -- (a) intends to adduce expert evidence at trial; or (b) becomes aware that
-- the party may adduce expert evidence at trial." (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to the Magistrates' Court unless
-- Magistrates' Court rules of court specify that the requirement ... applies".
-- Not one of the three courts: JUST FALSE (s 3 "court means").
GIVEN `the court`                                   IS A `Court`
      `the Magistrates' Court rules apply it`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intend or may adduce expert evidence at trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rules or the court provide otherwise`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65G -- I must seek the court's direction about expert evidence` `the court` `the Magistrates' Court rules apply it` `I intend or may adduce expert evidence at trial` `the rules or the court provide otherwise` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I intend or may adduce expert evidence at trial`) OR `the rules or the court provide otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the court`
         WHEN `the Supreme Court` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `the County Court` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `the Magistrates' Court` THEN
             IF `the Magistrates' Court rules apply it`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 65J(4): "Except by leave of the court, a party affected may not adduce evidence from any other expert witness on the
-- issues dealt with in the joint experts report." s 65O(1): "Except by leave of the court, a party to a proceeding may not
-- adduce evidence of any other expert witness on any issue arising in proceedings if, in relation to that issue -- (a) a
-- single joint expert has been engaged; or (b) a court appointed expert has been appointed."
-- Neither bar applies: NOTHING-kind *silent* (Part 4.6 does not bar it; directions under s 65H may limit it).
GIVEN `a joint experts report deals with the issue and affects me`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `a single joint expert is engaged on the issue`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court appointed expert is appointed on the issue`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has given leave`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 65J(4), 65O -- I may call another expert on the issue` `a joint experts report deals with the issue and affects me` `a single joint expert is engaged on the issue` `a court appointed expert is appointed on the issue` `the court has given leave` MEANS
    IF `a joint experts report deals with the issue and affects me` OR `a single joint expert is engaged on the issue` OR `a court appointed expert is appointed on the issue`
    THEN IF `the court has given leave`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 65L(6): "Any party who knows that a person is under consideration for engagement as a single joint expert -- (a) must
-- not, prior to the engagement, communicate with the person to obtain an opinion on the issues concerned; and (b) must
-- notify the other parties to the proceeding of the substance of any previous communications on the issues concerned."
-- Not knowing: JUST FALSE ("who knows", read as a "where" condition; fork F8). After the engagement: JUST FALSE for (a)
-- (a period the text fixes, "prior to the engagement").
GIVEN `I know the person is under consideration as a single joint expert` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been engaged`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65L(6)(a) -- I must not seek the person's opinion` `I know the person is under consideration as a single joint expert` `the person has been engaged` MEANS
    IF `I know the person is under consideration as a single joint expert` AND (NOT `the person has been engaged`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `I know the person is under consideration as a single joint expert` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have communicated with the person on the issues before`          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65L(6)(b) -- I must tell the other parties of my earlier communications` `I know the person is under consideration as a single joint expert` `I have communicated with the person on the issues before` MEANS
    IF `I know the person is under consideration as a single joint expert` AND `I have communicated with the person on the issues before`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 65N(1): "If a single joint expert is engaged or a court appointed expert is appointed in a proceeding, the parties to
-- the proceeding must endeavour to agree on -- (a) written instructions ...; and (b) the facts and assumptions of fact on
-- which the expert's report is to be based." (2): "If the parties cannot agree on any of the matters ..., the parties must
-- seek directions from the court."
GIVEN `a single joint or court appointed expert is engaged`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties have agreed the instructions and facts`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65N(2) -- I must seek directions on the expert's instructions` `a single joint or court appointed expert is engaged` `the parties have agreed the instructions and facts` MEANS
    IF `a single joint or court appointed expert is engaged` AND (NOT `the parties have agreed the instructions and facts`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 65P(1): "Unless rules of court otherwise provide, a party to a civil proceeding may apply to the court for an order
-- that an expert witness retained by any party ... disclose all or specified aspects of the arrangements under which the
-- expert witness has been retained". (4): "A party must not adduce evidence of a disclosure made pursuant to an order made
-- under this section at the trial without leave of the court."
GIVEN `the rules of court provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65P(1) -- I may apply for disclosure of an expert's retainer` `the rules of court provide otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the rules of court provide otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `the court has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65P(4) -- I may adduce evidence of the retainer disclosure at trial` `the court has given leave` MEANS
    IF `the court has given leave`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Chapter 5 -- appropriate dispute resolution (ss 3, 66, 67)`

-- s 3: "appropriate dispute resolution ... including, but not limited to -- (a) mediation ...; (b) early neutral
-- evaluation; (c) judicial resolution conference; (d) settlement conference; (e) reference ... to a special referee; (f)
-- expert determination; (g) conciliation; (h) arbitration".
DECLARE `Kind of appropriate dispute resolution` IS ONE OF
    `mediation`
    `early neutral evaluation`
    `a judicial resolution conference`
    `a settlement conference`
    `conciliation`
    `arbitration`
    `reference to a special referee`
    `expert determination`
    `another process with a binding outcome`
    `another process without a binding outcome`

-- s 66(2): "Subject to any rules of court, an order under subsection (1) may be made without the consent of the parties if
-- the type of appropriate dispute resolution ... is not -- (a) arbitration; or (b) reference to a special referee; or (c)
-- expert determination; or (d) any other type of appropriate dispute resolution which results, directly or indirectly, in
-- a binding outcome."
-- Rules of court providing otherwise: NOTHING-kind *points outside the text* (the rules are not deposited).
GIVEN `the kind`                             IS A `Kind of appropriate dispute resolution`
      `the rules of court provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(2) -- the court may send my case to dispute resolution without my consent` `the kind` `the rules of court provide otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the rules of court provide otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind`
         WHEN `arbitration` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `reference to a special referee` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `expert determination` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `another process with a binding outcome` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 67: "If a court orders that a judicial resolution conference be conducted ..., no evidence shall be admitted at the
-- hearing of any proceeding of anything said or done by any person in the course of the conduct of the judicial
-- resolution conference unless the court otherwise orders, having regard to the interests of justice and fairness."
-- A conference not ordered by the court: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*.
GIVEN `the conference was ordered by the court`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court orders otherwise`                IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67 -- what was said at the judicial resolution conference can be given in evidence` `the conference was ordered by the court` `the court orders otherwise` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the conference was ordered by the court`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the court orders otherwise`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
